  "content": "<p>A <strong>ratio</strong> compares quantities. To <strong>simplify</strong>, divide all parts by the HCF. To <strong>divide a quantity</strong> in a ratio: add the parts, find one part, then multiply.</p><p>The <strong>unitary method</strong>: find the value of one unit first, then scale up or down.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Share £240 in the ratio 3 : 5.</strong></p><p>Total parts = 8. One part = £30. Shares: £90 and £150.</p>"
